    verification prePushBehindCheckReviewGate : Test { :>> id = "6e3ccae5-1d2e-44bc-9127-56623c04f3d5"; :>> title = "Sprint 410 review gate — three passes per D0172"; :>> createdAt = "2026-08-22"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "PASS 1, CLAIMS: both push outcomes are exit codes from the scratch run in this session. PASS 2, BOUNDARY: an up-to-date-but-isolation-gated push still lands (the finding's own recorded caveat) - the hook forces the FETCH-INTEGRATE half of the loop and keel land remains the path of least resistance for the gate half; stated, not solved. PASS 3, OWN DIFF: the first scratch run's refusal came from the FETCH-FAILURE branch (the too-long path), not the behind branch - which would have been a false pass of the wrong path; caught by reading the message text, re-run cleanly. WHAT A REVIEWER SHOULD ATTACK: the hook trusts refs/heads/main as THE trunk name; a project with a different default branch gets no protection - one-line fix when it bites, named here."; }
